{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2","id":398609,"title":"Moving Up the Tiers 2!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T02:28:18-08:00","id":398609,"title":"Moving Up the Tiers 2!","content":"So lately I was thinking about reviving an old project of mine, in which I've made Conspiracy Endowments for compacts (which could be found in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies\">here</a>). While originally I've also added some story hook about how the compact changed its tier, I think that this time I won't do it- too limiting for ideas. Maybe I'll give a story hook or something, but nothing like a detailed background.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is the summary for the Endowments I've already made-<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey- Vice Projection:</b> the ability to influence, manipulate and change the dark passions of others to your will.<br /> <b>Long Night- Blessed Speech:</b> saving souls by using theological arguments and inspired words<br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule- </b><b>Das Archive:</b> a network of ghosts of fallen members who share their collective knowledge with the living<br /> <b>Null Mysteriis- Energetic Theories: </b>the ability to create devices powered by the &quot;supernatural energies&quot; of post human entities<br /> <b>The Union- HunterNet:</b> a special app which helps the members to unite and work together through the whole world<br /> <b>Division VI- Paradox Technologies:</b> special semi-living weaponry which disrupts the horrors of reality deviants.<br /> <b>Keepers of the Source- Green Magic:</b> using Ley Lines to channel the gifts of Mother Earth without harming the natural balance.<br /> <b>Bear Lodge: Spirit Hunt-</b> using the blessing of spiritual totems to increase the physical and mental abilities of the hunter<br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood: Sight Enhancers-</b> special drugs used to see and interact better with the unseen world while maintaining control<br /> <b>Talbot Group:</b> <b>Empathy-</b> the psychic ability to read and calm emotions<br /> <b>Barret Commission:</b> <b>Divine Right-</b> the ability to force your will upon power structure and use your authority as a weapon<br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: Sacred Blood-</b> invoking the aspects of the Great Goddess using holy blood magics<br /> <b>Night Watch: Hunt Zone-</b> marking your territory and creating a special bond with it, so you'll always get the upper hand<br /> <b>Habibti Ma: Justice's Touch-</b> purifying the mind and body from supernatural manipulations<br /> <b>Utopia Now: Spare Parts-</b> using stolen tech of the Machine, the user can create his own projects and servants<br /> <b>Les Voyageurs: </b><b>Enchanted Pelt-</b> by wearing the skin of her prey, the hunter can become one of them<br /> <b>Scarlet Watch: Bloody Binding- </b>connecting blood to blood and making it into a weapon against those who share it.<br /> <b>Ahl al Jabal:</b> <b>Hashshashin's Dance-</b> mystical trance which enhance the user's abilities and skills to an inhuman level<br /> <b>Heritage House:</b> <b>Legacy Coin-</b> a bitcoin like resource which allows the hunter to gain all kinds of favors from the families of the group- and even other organizations.<br /> <b>The Hunt Club:</b> <b>Second Face-</b> wearing a dark persona to avoid sins and gain the dark abilities of slashers while avoiding the price.<br /> <b>Ama San: Sea Song-</b> special song taught by the sea gods which rules the weather and lures their prey.<br /> <b>Azusa Miko: Kagura-</b> mystical dances which influence the kami to transform the world.<br /> <b>Bijin: Networking-</b>\u200b controlling information and gaining favors which help them artists gain their so much desired access<br /> <b>Gimu: Divine Grace-</b> manifestation of their inner duty and disciplines which guides their body and soul and focus<br /> their inner power.<br /> <b>Keepers of the Weave: Tale Binding-</b> drawing power from the old stories of mankind to confuse monsters and enhance allies<br /> <b>Protectors of the Light: Ward-</b> establishing a powerful link with the land in order to draw its power and protect it from the true enemy.<br /> <b>Yuri's Group: Lifebond-</b> by creating powerful bonds between each other, they can share each another's powers in order to support their friends.. and enemies.<br /> <b>Reckoning: Reverentia</b>- invocations of God's majesty and awe which strike fear in the hearts of the unfaithful and shatter their pride like Babel.<br /> <b>Phoenix Fire Guard: FP-</b> special equipment created thanks to Sheriff Brown's efforts which gives its deputies the ability to fight the Divine Fire and its abominations.<br /> <b>Tomb Raiders: Dream Gate-</b> the ability to open gates to the dream world of the Begotten and steal from there any treasure they see as fit.<br /> <br /> Mystery Cults:<br /> <b>Narodnaia Volia: Anarchy-</b> gaining tolerance against the vampire's slaving ability in order to steal the tyrants's power<br /> <b>Cult of Mitra: Divine Fate-</b> taking holy oath in front of the Wyld and becoming a character in a story- for better and worse.<br /> <b>Chosen of Mammon: Primal Utility-</b> for everything has a price, and they have the coin to pay for it<br /> <b>Siblings in Arms: Big Guns</b>- reverse engineered technology from the God Machine which feeds on the remains of dead spirits<br /> <b>Fellowship of the Finale Answer:</b> Anomaly- for time travel and not being a part of reality has its benefits<br /> <b>Church of Inti: Sunfire- </b>channeling the Essence of their god, their enemies would burn with the same fire which burns them<br /> <b>Voyagers: Kotoba no Kokai- </b>using words and blood, they can force their will upon the world with mystical ofudas<br /> <b>Tick Tock Men: Bioclock-</b> using a technological implement in order to enhance their speed to levels no mortal should be able to, and it has its consequences.<br /> <b>Cuauhualtin- Ihhuitzoncalli</b>: by creating a spiritual bond with his companion, the eagle warrior may touch the heavens<br /> <b>Ocelomeh- Cehualli:</b> embracing the shadows of the world, the dread jaguar warriors could slay their enemies with shaded fangs and claws<br /> <b>Nahualtin- Tezcatilpoca: </b>gifted by the Smoking Mirror, the priests of Mexica are able to channel dread magics known only to the wisest spellcasters, even if they need to taint their very soul.<br /> <b>Huitzilopotchli the Many Wheeled- Tonalpohualli:</b> many secrets are hidden in the holy calendar, and those who can read the sign and cycles of the world could channel its power and become one with their god.<br /> <b>Titgwai Gang- Gisei:</b> the ability to call upon the sacrifices given to the goddess of death and trains in times of need<br /> <br /> Skin &amp; Bones-<br /> <b>The Carvers:</b> <b>Persona</b><b>-</b> using their own strength of personality in order to turn the slasher's ego against him<br /> <b>The Dirge:</b> <b>Last Blow Serum- </b>a techno-magical serum contained in weapons used to make sure the dead won't rise again<br /> <b>The Silver Cross:</b> <b>Neo- Medicine- </b>secret, high tech surgery tools which allow to deal with almost any regular and supernatural injury.<br /> <b>The Wordsmiths:</b> <b>Psychological Supression</b>- the ability to remind the monsters they were once human, in the price of their potency.<br /> <b>Sons &amp; Daughters of Cheshire:</b> <b>Disruption Field-</b> shards of dark artifacts used to seal gates and stop other items fro working.<br /> <b>Terra Incognita:</b> <b>Cleaners-</b> a set of engineered botanic specimens which feeds upon the Divine Fire to grow<br /> <br /> Alchemist Guilds:<br /> <b>Lodowick Society: Divine Vision- </b>by following God's will and guidance, the hunters may summon visions of the future to help in the Vigil<br /> <b>Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice: Aludel-</b> alchemical items containing sparks of the Divine Fire to be used by those unworthy for the Art<br /> <b>Amalgama Ltd: Transhuman Potential-</b> using a combination of alchemy and biotechnology, the company's mercenaries change their body into killing machines.<br /> <b>Emerald Crucible: Amulet of Eternity-</b> a false &quot;philosopher's stone&quot; which gives those who wear it a chance to stave off death itself<br /> <b>Order of the Four Cornered Seal: Gu-</b> using an heretic ceremony which refined venom into power in the price of mental and physical balance.<br /> <br /> Companies:<br /> <b>Last Dynasty International: Infused Pharmaceuticals- </b>drugs enhanced by Sekhem which reinforce the body and heal injuries<br /> <b>Deva Corporation: Luminous Advancements- </b>being part of a great Infrastructure, they can draw power from the Machine for their benefit<br /> <b>White Heart Pharmaceuticals: Paranormal Infections-</b> special diseases developed using occult formulas and strange pathogens which use their hunter as host<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Cults:<br /> <b>Tauran: Calls of Earth-</b> evoking the affinity the members of the order has with the earth and mountains in order to shape the world around them<br /> <b>Adelfoi Aimatos: Blood Curses-</b> dangerous rituals which could cast a dread curse upon anyone the sorcerer has their blood and name<br /> <b>\u200bLoyalists of the Ptolemaic Dynasty: Entombment-</b> special ceremony which allows the user to cross the veil between life and death in order to become more like their undying Mistress<br /> <b>Parangelia Seth: Isfet-</b> terrible ability to twist Sekhem out of form and craft it into a temporary relic, in exchange for cursing the world around them<br /> <b>Strangers: Golden Apple-</b> special recipes which allow transforming regular fruits into magical conducts of power, granting inhuman abilities to chosen heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-21-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T06:29:20-08:00","id":398735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2#post398609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ahl al Jabal:</b> <b>Hashshashin's Dance-</b> mystical trance which enhance the user's abilities and skills to an inhuman level<br /> <b>Bear Lodge: Spirit Hunt-</b> using the blessing of spiritual totems to increase the physical and mental abilities of the hunter<br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: Sacred Blood-</b> invoking the aspects of the Great Goddess using holy blood magics<br /> <b>Night Watch: Hunt Zone-</b> marking your territory and creating a special bond with it, so you'll always get the upper hand<br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood: Sight Enhancers-</b> special drugs used to see and interact better with the unseen world while maintaining control<br /> <b>Talbot Group:</b> <b>Empathy-</b> the psychic ability to read and calm emotions</div> </div> </div> </div>These sound good. Though I think the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood shouldn't need a <i>lot</i> of blood - as in not damaging amounts, just a few drops (but they have to draw it then and there, which takes time and something sharp).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Barret Commission:</b> <b>Flow of Power-</b> a weird sense which allows to see and manipulate structures of power. </div> </div> </div>Something based on the divine right of kings, maybe, but with a much broader definition of king?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Hunt Club:</b> <b>Black Token-</b> a dark network of people and machines who use a special coin to escape punishment and get anything </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest something more like murder trophies - not too dissimilar to the boosts the Bear Lodge get, but the slasher is their own totem. One of the benefits ought to be the sliding off of consequences though - by putting yourself above the world of the ordinary people, the powers of their world can't touch you, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Utopia Now: Spare Parts-</b> using stolen tech of the Machine, the user can create his own projects and servants </div> </div> </div>Stolen designs - they don't need to steal each and every component (though they would need to for R&amp;D).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:40:40-08:00","id":400136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=398735#post398735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These sound good. Though I think the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood shouldn't need a <i>lot</i> of blood - as in not damaging amounts, just a few drops (but they have to draw it then and there, which takes time and something sharp).</div> </div> </div> </div>that was what I've had in mind. Hurting themselves for power isn't really what I think they should be doing. Their magic should be about life.. unless they take the form of the Crone (I kinda think their Endowment should be split into 3 &quot;spheres&quot;, one for each Aspect of the Goddess- Maiden, Mother and Crone, with one for enchanting, one for healing and one for actually doing some damage)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something based on the divine right of kings, maybe, but with a much broader definition of king? </div> </div> </div>sounds interesting- something like using your &quot;divine right&quot; in order to command large groups, forcing supernatural laws or simply using the fact that you are &quot;higher&quot;, and so should be obeyed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd suggest something more like murder trophies - not too dissimilar to the boosts the Bear Lodge get, but the slasher is their own totem. One of the benefits ought to be the sliding off of consequences though - by putting yourself above the world of the ordinary people, the powers of their world can't touch you, that sort of thing. </div> </div> </div>That's actually cool. The reason I didn't went to something mystical was because I wanted to brainstorm some more &quot;mundane&quot; Endowments- but the idea of using a Slasher persona in order to hide your sins away from you is interesting. Maybe something like enjoying the benefit of certain Undertakings without actually falling to slasherhood?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stolen designs - they don't need to steal each and every component (though they would need to for R&amp;D). </div> </div> </div>That was more or less what I've thought about- you use reverse engineering in order to understand the machine, and then start using some specialized version of Resources in order to create your own things. The problem is that in order to replenish your dots, you have to go and tear some of the God Machine's projects down- like angels, demons, cryptids, Infrastructures and other GM tech.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:52:24-08:00","id":400729,"title":"","content":"The ones that interest me is the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood (and if they don't get bonuses for using actual maiden's blood <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and the Barret Commission. Though the later is because I have a somewhat similar concept that could use the inspiration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:39:52-08:00","id":400856,"title":"","content":"I'll start making things after my finales. For now, it is just for brainstorming.<br /> <br /> Also, if we are talking about giving Endowments for orgs who don't have it, here is my idea for Endowments used by other powerful groups in the World of Darkness-<br /> <br /> <b>Last Dynasty International: Infused Pharmaceuticals- </b>drugs enhanced by Sekhem which reinforce the body and heal injuries<br /> <b>Deva Corporation: Luminous Advancements- </b>being part of a great Infrastructure, they can draw power from the Machine for their benefit<br /> <b>Iron Comrades</b> (don't like the name, but what can I do?)<b> : </b><b>Process</b> <b>KRASNYY-</b> manipulating the essence of a captures creature to develop psychic abilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T14:07:34-08:00","id":405060,"title":"","content":"So, here comes the Spirit Slayers!<br /> <br /> <b>Bear Lodge- Spirit Hunt </b>(1-5, special)<br /> In order to become the best hunters around, the Lodge had bonded itself with powerful hunt spirits- especially the Thunder Bear- in order to bring down shape-shifters. That Endowment is divided into 9 Aspects of the Bear, with each corresponding to a different Attribute: Fang (Strength), Claw (Dexterity), Hide (Stamina), Roar (Presence), Eye (Manipulation), Heart (Composure), Head (Intelligence), Nose (Wits) and Silence (Resolve). Each such Aspect is rated between 1 to 5 as a separate Endowment. In order to use the Endowment, the user must first decide upon a certain target and promise it as a sacrifice to the Thunder Bear's spirit court. Once the rite is complete, the hunter may add her dots in each Aspect to the corresponding Attribute- but only when dealing against the target. The hunter may also target a group instead of a single being. When the rite is preformed, the hunter must declare a time limit to the Spirit Hunt, which can be no longer then one day per Status: Bear Lodge dot. While under the effect of the Aspects, the hunter may also interact with entities in the Shadow Frequency of the Twilight.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood: Sight Enhancers </b>(1-5)<br /> Thanks to an advanced chemical research, the members of the brotherhood discovered a way to interact with the Shadow more efficiently. First, under those drugs, the hunter have full control over her action. Second, she enjoys the benefit of the Unseen Sense (Spirit) Merit. Third, the hunter may see into the Twilight and even behind the Gauntlet. The dots in the Endowment represent the quality of the drug- which effects the character for one hour per dot. Plus, it represent how well does the character interact with spirits-<br /> 1- sight<br /> 2- hearing<br /> 3- speak with<br /> 4- touch<br /> 5- step sideways (when the effect of the drug ends, the hunter immediately returns to the material world)<br /> In an addition to those effect, each such drug has a side effect. Each time you take such a drug, you choose a single spirit Numina. As long as you under its effect, you can use that Numina freely.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group:</b> <b>Empathy </b>(1-5, special)<br /> After dealing a lot of time among troubled people, a psychic sense has started to developed among the people of the Group. First, simply having a dot in the Endowment allows the hunter to feel the surface emotions of a certain person. Second, choose a certain emotion (like sadness, hope, fear, rage, love, etc). By rolling [Empathy + Manipulation], the character may trigger that emotion inside someone or calm that specific emotion. That roll may be protected by using Willpower or the Supernatural Resistance trait as normal. A special thing about that Endowment is that no matter which emotion chosen, it could be used in order to calm down someone who is under the effect of a supernatural emotion manipulation (including vampire's Frenzy, werewolf's Death Rage, a person under the effect of a Disquiet or even other uses of Empathy). The requires rolling a Clash of Wills between the dots in the chosen Endowment against the trait who is responsible for the emotional manipulation (like Blood Potency in case of vampires, or the other Empathy trait in case of two hunters). Finally, the hunter may use her dots in her highest Empathy as a Supernatural Resistance trait when trying to protect against an emotional manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T10:33:11-08:00","id":405914,"title":"","content":"And now- Night Stalkers<br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: Sacred Blood (1-5, special)</b><br /> By embracing their occult nature and the influence of their witches, the Sisterhood has found a way to invoke the Aspects of the Triple Goddess through their blood. By spilling a bit of blood (not enough to actually count as damage, but it requires them to at least scratch themselves), the Sister can enjoy the advantages of the Maiden, the Mother or the Crone. If the user is a Maiden (that is, virgin- yes, oral sex counts), she gains +2 modifier to all rolls when using the Aspects. If the user is a male, he suffer -2 modifier to all rolls. Each of the three Aspects is bought as a separate Endowment, and has a different effect-<br /> <b>Maiden</b>- the Sister can heal others with her presence. By rolling [Maiden+ Presence], she may heal one level of Lethal damage per success. Exceptional Success makes it into 2 levels healed, and a Dramatic Failure means causing one level of Bashing damage per dot in Maiden<br /> <b>Mother</b>- the Sister can influence the emotions of others. By rolling [Mother+ Manipulation] she can force upon someone the Attached Condition in relation to her for one hour per Mother. Exceptional Success means 2 hours per dot and Dramatic Failure means that the target would see the Sister as an enemy<br /> <b>Crone</b>- wearing the Aspect of death, the Sister can return the unliving to where they belong. By attacking an undead (or deathless) creature she can add her dots in Crone to the attack roll. If the Attack is successful, the undead suffer one level of additional Aggravated Damage per dot in Crone<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: Hunt Zone (1-5, special)</b><br /> The Hunt Zone is where the hunter would always have the higher hand, and any vampire trapped in his turf is better to prepare himself to a die. Each such Hunt Zone is bought separately, and requires spending blood in the form of one level of lethal damage once a month on a place called &quot;The Focus&quot;. The area in the radius of 5 meters per dots of the Focus is called the Hunt Zone. As long as the hunter is in the Hunt Zone, he may add the dots of the specific Zone to all of his rolls. Plus, he enjoys the effect of the Clairvoyance merit in order to see anything which happens in his Zone. Also, the Hunter may instal a number of traps equal to his dots in his Zone which would be activated by spending a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Barret Commission:</b> <b>Divine Right (1-5)</b><br /> The hunter is a king by all but the name, and both Heaven and Earth recognize his right to rule. First, the hunter may add his dots in the Divine Right to all of his social rolls. Second, for each dot in his Endowment the hunter may command a Decree. While he may change Decrees freely, they can never have more in the same time then his dots in the Divine Right. Anyone who is officially beneath the hunter in hierarchy must obey the Decrees, unless it should end up in direct damage to himself. Supernatural creatures who have a Resistance trait may try to use Clash of Wills to ignore the effect against the hunter's dot in the Endowment. The hunter may try to force someone who isn't officially below him to obey his Decrees, but then he must roll for [Manipulation + Divine Right] against a Willpower roll.<br /> <br /> This Endowment also has another special effect. Every time the sun set, choose one of the three Predatory Auras. You can project that Aura at the cost of a Willpower point. Replace Blood Potency with Divine Right when relevant. Vampires, as well as any creature who can be effected by such Auras, would react to them.<br /> <br /> EDIT- and eventually, switched Mother and Maiden to how I've first wrote them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-09-2016, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T04:42:17-08:00","id":406591,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains-<br /> <br /> <b>Habibti Ma: Justice's Touch (1-5)</b><br /> Thanks to the blessing of the mysterious Maat, you manage to free people from brainwashing- both magical and mundane. By touching the target, the victim is rolling Willpower + Justice (use the victim's Willpower score. You can only help him fight back, not do the ob for him) against the controller's Supernatural trait if there is such (as regular for Clash of Wills). Success means that the victim was deprogrammed, removing any Condition which once bound him. If it was a supernatural effect, it is terminated in the same moment- a possessing spirit is separated from the body, blood bonds are broken, hypnosis is no more. Exceptional Success means that the victim is also now immune to any form on mental manipulation or reprogramming/brainwashing for a month. Dramatic Failure reprogram the victim again, gives him a certain Condition to the ST's choosing. You also add your dots in the Endowment to resist any attempt to brainwash or manipulate you.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now: Spare Parts (1-5)</b><br /> By stealing enough of the God Machine's tech, you are now able to make things of your own. The dots in the Endowment are used as a special Resources dots, which represent you access to the hardware found in the Conspiracy's storage. Using those dots and by accessing the labs, you can make an temporary device powered up bu the energy of the Machine. If the device has a limited number of uses, it is limited to three use per dot in the Endowment. If not, it lasts for one week per dot. Your dots in the Endowment dictate what you can create-<br /> 1- Embedded Gadget<br /> 2- Exploited Gadget<br /> 3- a device mimicking Stigmatic merits<br /> 4- a device mimicking Demonic Form abilities<br /> 5- an angel<br /> The rating of the Embed, Exploit or the number of Form Abilities in the device can't be higher then your dots in the Endowment. Creating an Angel would require rolling Manipulation against the Rank of the angel every time you give it a mission. Success means it would obey. Exceptional Success means it would obey and not resist for the rest of the missions. Failure means it would not obey, and suffer 2 levels of Aggravated damage. Dramatic Failure means one of the following- either it would escape and reconnects to the Machine, or that it would fall. In order to enjoy free access to the storage of the conspiracy, you are expected to bring their offices something in the level of your dots in the Endowment once per month (so if you make an army of angels, you better start hunting a lot of those)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:43:24-08:00","id":409862,"title":"","content":"Infused Pharmaceuticals: I think it would be worth just duplicating Elixirs here; maybe not the exact individual ones, but LDI and the AO come from the same part of the world and draw on the same historical and magical traditions, so mechanical differentiation is pointless. Instead, differentiate them in attitude: LDI's elixirs aren't sacred mysteries for initiates, but like thaumotech, repurposed failures; successes are those that can be used by (and thus sold to) anyone, not those dependent on an exacting regimen to metabolise.<br /> <br /> Sight Enhancers: Might the user also become attractive to spirits, so they gradually congreate around her (and maybe at the fifth level become a quasi-locus so spirits - and werewolves - can cross the gauntlet more easily in her presence)?<br /> <br /> Sacred Blood: My instinct would be to swap the Maiden and Mother round. (Also to say that a male virgin has the two modifiers cancel out).<br /> <br /> Divine Right: Pretty much exactly what I had in mind.<br /> <br /> Justice's Touch: I like this one; I especially like that it doesn't particularly distinguish between natural and supernatural forms of conditioning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:09:57-08:00","id":410464,"title":"","content":"Glad you liked it! About LDI- it is simply a thought about expanding the revivals from Dark Eras. Making the fifth level of the Sight Enhancer into making you into a Loci could work- it is simply that I've thought that it correlates with &quot;getting lost in your minds&quot; from a drug that &quot;powerful&quot;. Maybe I could mix the two effects together. As for Sacred Blood- I am also not that sure about which effect should be Mother and which should be Maiden, so it is open for changes. The reason for the penalty for male users is because the group is feminist, so it made sense that in the same way that men can't rise their Status too much, they also can invoke the Aspects of the Goddess in the same efficiency (except of the Crone, which is an Attack roll). Glad you liked the other two- and yeah, considering that saving cultists from brainwash is the thing for the Habibi Ma, it made sense for their Endowment to effect any kind of conditioning.<br /> <br /> Now, while I do have a clear vision of the Scarlet Watch's Endowments, I'm not sure about the Les Voyageurs. How can I make Wolf's Pelt into something which doesn't simply turns them into Skin Thieves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:33:24-08:00","id":414501,"title":"","content":"So while I'm tinkering about the Pelt Endowment, here are few ruff ideas for how those compacts has grown into conspiracies-<br /> <br /> the Bear Lodge- seeing the mortals who dared to hunt the hunters of the Shadow, the old spirit found itself interested. It was an ancient being, and lived to see the father of those spirit bastards fall by their own hands in the time before time. While it didn't had offspring of its own, it felt compelled to offer its help to the hunters, giving them a portion of its strength and so making a lineage of its own. Already naming themselves after him, the great Thunder Bear blessed the hunters with its own might- and now there is no greater hunter then them.<br /> <br /> Illuminated Brotherhood- it was only a matter of experimentation. Eventually, the Brotherhood managed to create or identify a group of drugs which allowed regular people to commune with the Shadow. Thanks to that breakthrough, the Brotherhood has started to sell those drugs, making enough money which allowed them to grow in influence and investigate the unseen.<br /> <br /> Talbot Group- being so close to the spirit world has eventually made the senses of the Group more keen. Their &quot;psychic gift&quot; is a result of long trainings and understanding of their patients, which eventually unlocked that inner potential. Thanks to their gift, their services as psychologies became a great resource.<br /> <br /> Maiden Blood Sisterhood- after their witches has captured a vampire who claimed connection to the Great Goddess, the secret rites were created to help those who weren't Awakened to higher mysteries. Their ability to actually do hedge magic has made them into an influential feminist neo-pagan group, especially thanks to their Endowment.<br /> <br /> Night Watch- a mysterious figure showed up before the group, claiming to know the secret ability to influence the city and become one with it. It taught the members some of its blood magic in exchange for protection. With their enhanced ability to rule the city, they were able to either force hunters out or made them into a part of the group. This is their turf- and you are either with them or the hell out of here.<br /> <br /> Barret Commission- already having members in key places in the government, it was only a matter of time until they rose to greatness. The fact that people listen to them isn't some kind of magic- it is their inborn right to rule. The secret item at safe 1-700-675-40 is not relevant.<br /> <br /> Habibi Ma- after breaking a cult big enough and forcing their deathless master to sleep in an epic fight, Maat has revealed itself in the heart of the people. Together with the former cultists, who already had knowledge and influence, and the gift of lady Justice after breaking the cursed relics, the group was able to have enough resources to free people all around the world<br /> <br /> Utopia Now- finally the group has managed to collect enough resources from the Machine and crack its designs through reverse engineering. It was a matter of time, after all- either the Machine would have caught them, or that they were to break its code. Thankfully, the former happened first- and now God is so kind that it sends them hunter angels every day. There is no such thing as too much Spare Parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T18:29:35-08:00","id":414729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=400856#post400856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Iron Comrades</b> (don't like the name, but what can I do?)<b> : </b><b>Process</b> <b>KRASNYY-</b> manipulating the essence of a captures creature to develop psychic abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you can, with good conscience. The Soviet Union wasn't big on poetic names like that, they mostly used project codes. Iconic names like Hind and Typhoon are NATO call signs for the things. It is likely, more than likely even, that Iron Comrades is just a nickname, either by soviets who had to deal with them, and got tired of not having a name on them, or NATO agents needing something to call them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:16:21-08:00","id":417547,"title":"","content":"going back in time, I present to you the compacts of the Dark Eras!<br /> <br /> <b>Enchanted Pelt </b>(1-5)<br /> in order to become a good hunter, one needs to learn to think like its prey- and what better way you have then becoming like it! The Les Voyageurs have learned the primal rites which allow man to wear the form of a beast- even is the beast is a mad chimera. The Pelt is a single relic which can work only for its maker, and which is made out of the skins of number of animals. By wearing the Pelt, the character can change her form into one of the extra forms a shapeshifter can take (that is, Beast, Near Beast, Hybrid and Near Man). Each such form is presented by the rating of the Endowment- Beast requires 1 dot, Near form requires 2 dots and Hybrid 3 dots. In order to take that form, the pelt must contain the skin of the desired animal. In theory, one could also buy new &quot;human&quot; forms, but you can understand why most hunters won't do it.. unless they'll fall into the shadows.<br /> <br /> While in Hybrid form, the hunter can also use Dominions, which are bought separately. The hunter can't have more Dominions then her dots in the Pelt. While the hunter can change the forms and Dominions of her Pelt as long as the new outcome answers the limitations, the hunter must roll Crafts to do so. Dramatic Failure means that the Pelt has been harmed, and you either loose one dot in the Endowment (the Sanctify of Merits is valid). Exceptional Success means that you can add one free Dread Power which can be used in any form of the Pelt, even if the number of Dominions is above the limit. If you roll Dramatic Failure afterward, however, you loose that free Dread Power (but you don't loose the dot in the Pelt).<br /> <br /> <b>Bloody Binding</b>(1-5)<br /> Blood calls to blood, and through that connection you have recovered the lost occult rites of your compact. By making a blood oath (that is, opening a wound in both you and another character), you gain a sympathetic connection to the target. You can't have more Blood Bounds then your dots in the Endowment. The connection between you and the Blood Bound allows you to always know the general place of the target and her general condition- if she is healthy, harmed, terrified, under mental compulsion or dead. The connection is not broken by death, but it is connected to the body, not the soul. The character can at any moment, break that connection, although it can't last more then 2 years per dot in the Endowment.<br /> <br /> In addition to the Blood Bound which are gained by the Endowment, and character which is a first degree relative (that is siblings, parents and children) are also targeted by the Endowment, and so does anyone which has consumed your or your Blood Bounds' blood until it is out of their system (for a living being, it is around an hour. For a vampire or any other being which collects the blood, it is until the Vitae is expanded). For the target of the Endowment, &quot;consuming the blood&quot; means that it entered the body of the target in any possible way.<br /> <br /> In additions for the Empathic conncetion, the Endowment also allows the character to add her dots in the Endowment to any rolls of Manipulation and attack rolls which are done against the target. The exception is the case of family members, which are immune to those effects unless they were also Blood Bound by the effects of the Endowment directly or has consumed the character's blood. In the case that the blood was consumed or that it was Blood Bound, the character may at any moment &quot;burn&quot; her blood, dealing one level of Aggravated Damage per dot in the Endowment. That effect destroys the empathic connection and breaks the Blood Binding.<br /> <br /> The effects of Blood Binding also extend to any being who steals the vitality of another, like the Owls or psychic vampires. It also allows that character to buy Telepathy and Extraordinary Perception Psychic Merits, although those function only toward targets who were Blood Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:24:14-08:00","id":417648,"title":"","content":"Also, decided to switch Maiden and Mother. It really works better thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:21:27-08:00","id":419135,"title":"","content":"and now all the orphans who were left behind<br /> <br /> <b>Hashshashin's Dance </b>(1-5)<br /> by using a combination of meditation, drugs and prayer, the hunter is ready to fight his Holy War against the abominations of the night. Roll a Meditation roll and add your dots in the Endowment for the Dicepooll. In case of Dramatic Failure, the hunter loose control and starts attacking anyone in sight. A Success means the hunter may choose one of the following Modes- Knife (or attack mode), Cloak (or defense mode), Stone (or health mode), Candle (or resistance mode) or Crown (for mental mode). The hunter then gains a bonus equal to the number of Successes according to the desired Mode for 2 hours per dot in the Dance (only one Mode can be activated is any time)<br /> Knife- add the bonus to attack rolls<br /> Cloak- add the bonus to the defense trait<br /> Stone- add a number of Health levels equal to the bonus<br /> Candle- you the bonus as a supernatural resistance trait<br /> Crown- add the bonus to any mental skill roll<br /> Exceptional Success means that the duration is doubled.<br /> <br /> <b>Legacy Coin </b>(1-5)<br /> family means everything- including giving you everything you need, and the House has made a special coin which would help you in getting what you need. Treat your dots in the Endowment as a second Resources Merit, but one which is specialized in getting things which are required to the Vigil. While weapons and ammo are the most common use, one could also pay with it to a certain hotel which helps hiding hunters, informants and snitches who hold precious intelligence and exotic ingredients like the banes of spirits and even the Endowments of other conspiracies (those who take a physical form). That coin may be used at any major hunter organization, although they can also use it to buy your services. It is for the Storyteller to decide which compacts and conspiracies has joined the House, but consider the following as &quot;canon&quot;- TF:V, Lucifuge, Ascending Ones, Cheiron Group, AKD, MM, VASCU, the Union, Null Mysteriis, Network Zero, Ashwood Abbey, Barret Commission, Night Watch, Utopia Now and the Scarlet Watch (if they still exist in your setting). In case you wish to buy an Endowment, you must have 2+[Desired Endowment's rating] dots in the Coin. If the Endowment is consumable (like Elixirs or certain Advanced Armory), you need you buy them again and again but coming to the &quot;office&quot; of the desired organization.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Face</b> (1-5)<br /> the horrible power of the Hunt Club comes from their ability to through their sins upon another personality which sleeps inside their minds and awaken only when called to the hunt. Each such Endowment is based around a Slasher Undertaking. By expanding Willpower point, the hunter may awaken that hidden self. The hunter must choose a single Undertaking when expanding the Willpower, and can't change it until the effect is ended. If the hunter has 1-3 dots in the Endowment, he enjoys the benefits (and suffer the frailties) of the Ripper Undertaking. If he has more then 3, however, he may choose the Scourge one. While wearing his new &quot;face&quot;, the hunter does not need to roll Integrity for any breaking point which is equal or lower then his dots in the Endowment. The effect of the Endowment lasts for a number of hours equal to the dots of the Endowment, although after killing a victim the hunter may choose to end it freely. If the hunter wish to end the effect without killing, he mus roll Willpower. Success means that the effect is terminated. Exceptional Success means that the next time the hunter wishes to end the hunt without killing he can do so without the roll. Failure means that the effect is still on, and while the hunter may try again he suffer -1 modifier for any previous attempt. Dramatic Failure means that the hunter must kill the first victim his Slasher persona targets he finds in his way, and then the effect is terminated.<br /> <br /> While in theory the hunter can simply wait for the effect to leave naturally, as long as he didn't killed a victim he must roll Willpower every hour. Failure and Dramatic Failure are equal to the previous roll. Success means that he doesn't need to kill in this hour. Exceptional Success means that the hunter doesn't need to roll for the rest of the duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> and with it, I finish with the canon groups. Next time, the big orgs who are conspiracies in all but the name! Also- anyone has a suggestion for more groups other then the 3 that I've listed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:37:28-08:00","id":425248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=417648#post417648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, decided to switch Maiden and Mother. It really works better thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I was just coming to say I'd been wrong to suggest doing that. Given the group's usual MO, the emotional influence is most likely to be used for calming down victims and getting people to trust them, which is very Motherly - meanwhile, one of the Maiden's images is that of being vibrantly alive, which squares with healing.<br /> <br /> I like the snippets of history you gave everyone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:48:29-08:00","id":425252,"title":"","content":"and that was my initial thought.... well, this is an homebrew, so I guess anyone can decide what is better for their game :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:48:54-07:00","id":625838,"title":"","content":"so after 13 straight days of learning to tests, my brain is on the verge of exploding- so there is a good chance I'll take a little break and do something creative. Considering that we got the writeups of the 6 Edo period groups, I plan on giving supernatural Endowments to the 4 compacts presented there (and maybe finally giving ones to the 3 orgs presented in the beginning). Some of the compacts are easy to think about a proper Endowment- the Ama San already have their Sea Whistle, and the Azusa Miko come with a strong foundation in Shinto and Japanese shamanism so thinking about an Endowment for them shouldn't be that hard. The Gimu require some thought, for giving them Kewel Sword Powerz is exactly what I shouldn't do. Instead, I was thinking about giving them Paladin like powers- that is, something which makes them draw mystical power from their own duty to their country and people. The Bijin present a dilemma- I'm not sure if their Endowment should revolve around their art, maybe as a form of inspiration, or around their gossip sharing and information manipulation. Personally, I'll go with the later, but maybe you have your own suggestions.<br /> <br /> opinions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T11:33:26-07:00","id":633619,"title":"","content":"<b>Ama San- Sea Song (0-00000)</b><br /> While the Sea Whistle is the most common technique for luring the monsters of the deep, the Sea Song is a more delicate and powerful ability. Taught by the great Ryujin, the Sea Song can effect the sea and sky to calm storms and strength the waves. The sea Song has a number of uses- the first is enhancing the ability of the Sea Whistle, represented by adding the dots in the Endowment to the dicepool. That effect may influence even no sea monsters, but you reduce 2 dice from the roll. Second, it allows the hunter to control the weather- by rolling Endowment+Presence and paying 1 WP point per dot in the Endowment (you can reduce your dicepool to save WP), the user may either make the weather more stormy or more calm. Consider a &quot;bright day&quot; as 0, &quot;rainy&quot; as 1, &quot;warm&quot; as -1, &quot;stormy&quot; as 2 and &quot;heat wave&quot; as -2. you can't move between more states in the same time than your dots in the Endowment. Exceptional Success gives the WP back and Dramatic Failure turns the Weather the other way around. Finally, you can buy Dread Powers which are connected to sea monsters- but no more than one Power per dot in the Endowment.<br /> <br /> <b>Azusa Miko- Kagura (0-00000, special)</b><br /> the bow shamans of Edo have learned the ways of spirits for hundreds of years, and by using their sacred dance they can bestow the gifts of their gods without being used as their pawns. Using the sacred dance, the priestess may transform the spirit world- and by doing so, the world of flesh. Each Kagura is based around a single Influence, and the Miko has an Essence pool equal to their Status. In order to activate the Endowment, the hunter must roll the Kagura+Performance, and if she Succeed she may spend Essence to activate the effects of the Influence up to her dots in the Kagura. She may regain Essence by meditation, maintaining a weekly taboo or as a gift of service from a ghost or a spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Bijin- Networking (0-00000)</b><br /> as masters of manipulations and information control, the Beautiful Ones can play a delicate game of influence over the monsters. The hunter needs to target a certain target and make a conversation with it, and than roll Endowment+Manipulation. Success means the hunter gains out of the target a number of favors, connections and wealth, as represented by a number of temporary Merit dots which can be spread among Allies, Resources, Contacts and any similar Social merit. Those Merits can only be used once, and after that the target is freed from its Favor. A target which tries to deny access to the Favor suffer for -1 per dot in the Endowment for the use of Social skills until she repays the Favor. An Exceptional Success means that the number of dots in doubled, while Dramatic Failure means that the hunter owes the target a Favor equal to their dots in the Endowment. The Merit dots gained by the Endowment must be connected to the target and to its status- you can't make a poor peasant give you Resources of 5, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Gimu- Divine Grace (0-00000)</b><br /> The samurai is protected by his owner and commitment, guided by his own Code of Life. As long as the hunter follows the Boshido and don't break his devotion, At the beginning of every Scene he may spend 1 WP and add his dots in the Endowment to his Defense, Attack rolls, Health (as temporary levels) or to any Skill he possess. The effects lasts until the end of the Scene. Breaking the code ends up with the hunter losing access to the Endowment until he restores his honor. The ST should be the one to decide which act may be considered as such &quot;redemption&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 08-20-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:05:47-07:00","id":633773,"title":"","content":"<b>Last Dynasties International- Infused Pharmaceuticals (0-00000)</b><br /> a product of long research and occult knowledge, the members of LDI may enhance their mind, body and soul using special formulas. For one day per dot of Status (which represent the quality of the pharmaceutical in question) the hunter may spread her dots in the Endowment between her attributes, temporary increasing them. The choice may not be changed until the end of the duration. In an addition, an hunter may get access to a special pharmaceutical which grants Dread Powers which their total dot worth is not higher than her dots in the Endowment. The hunter gets access to the Dread Power for one hour per dot in the Endowment and may &quot;recharge&quot; her elixir once every [10-Status] days.<br /> <br /> <b>Deva Corporation- Luminous Advancements (0-00000)</b><br /> being a part of a great Infrastructure, the hunter may channel its might through her and gain special Advancements for her used. In order to use the Endowment, the hunter must first &quot;tune&quot; to a certain Infrastructure, which requires rolling Endowment+Occult. Success means that the hunter may gain a number of Dread Powers equal to their dots in the Endowments, which are decided by the ST as powers which may advance the goal of the Infrastructure. The hunter stays tuned to the Infrastructure for one day per dot in the Endowment, although she may &quot;tune off&quot; at any moment. She may not be tuned to more than one Infrastructure at a time. The Dread Powers manifested by the hunter are usually manifested in the form of mechanical items or technological devices which may be operated only by the hands of the hunter. Exceptional Success means the duration is doubled. Failure gives a -1 modifier to any roll for tuning to the same Infrastructure in the same day. Dramatic Failure means an angel would be sent to investigate the &quot;security breach&quot; and deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:08:12-07:00","id":633777,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Care Bear Lodge( sorry, I couldn't resist) :<br /> <br /> -Is there any visible effect when the Endowment is active (like partial shapeshifting)? <br /> -What happens when a member fails to deliver a prey to the totem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:14:10-07:00","id":633780,"title":"","content":"there is no mundane visible effect, but those who can see through the Gauntlet would notice the shape of a great bear hovering above them. Even those who can see through the Twilight would notice the bear's shadow, and Unseen Senses related to spirits would be triggered by this Endowment. If the Spirit Hunt is failed the totem won't punish them, but I assume that they failure would crush their spirit- that is, they would lose a WP point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:20:19-07:00","id":633785,"title":"","content":"Mmmm... nice. I would include, in case of a repeating offender , to negate the use of the Endowment until said member furfils a difficult task/sacrifice for the totem.<br /> And about the Azusa Miko, can they use their Essence in other ways beside the Endowment, like activating fetishes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:24:46-07:00","id":633792,"title":"","content":"I think they would have to get a Merit in order to do so. The Essence is shaped especially for the Kaguya- any other use would require a new technique for shaping it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:33:26-07:00","id":633800,"title":"","content":"Also, the reason I won't give such penalty to the hunters of the Lodge is because<i> it is ok to fail</i>. Bear is a totem who believes that patience is a virtue, and you better run away from a fight you can't win to survive for another day. It would not punish its hunters for not being able to defeat an enemy they have chosen- sure, they may be prideful, but pride is good. It makes you dream big. The problem is not evaluating your opponent during the battle and choosing to fight to death instead to escape and thinking about a new strategy. While Bear may have punished those who didn't made the right choice, it usually doesn't need to- they end up dead.<br /> At least, that's how I view their totem. I won't send the homebrew police after you for not doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T14:30:05-08:00","id":797509,"title":"","content":"so- few more story hooks for how compacts would turn into conspiracies:<br /> <br /> Les Voyageurs- as fur merchants and hunters, they already had a good source of income. While the demand for the fur of wild animals did decreased with the years, the high class still knew how to appreciate good cloth- especially one made from mythical beasts and monsters. As the group started to invest all their resources in fashion business, their hunters has made contact with a group of native shamans who taught them a variation of the old skin-walking ritual. While today many animals are protected, one can't protect one beast from another- and thanks to the gifts of their ritual they may even stand as equals to their preferred prey- werewolves.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Watch- Salem is an hard time, yet the contract of the Watch is stronger. While the families has fell from greatness and the vampires hunt the members as much as they can while Cheiron absorbs the high class members of the group, the contract was still maintained. Blood and Fate bind that compact together, and Blood and Fate allowed them to discover their old rites and returned them to their former status.<br /> <br /> Ahl al Jabal- the people of the mountain has always practiced occult methods in order to enhance their souls against the night. All it needed for them was a reason to grow- and the Arab Spring was just that. With the Syrian Civil War tearing their lands apart and the chaos which roams in Iraq, more and more people seek for a meaning, for a way to protect themselves both from human and supernatural evil, and the Ahl al Jabal has started to represent just that- a way for one to protect himself from the dark with the blessings of God.<br /> <br /> Heritage House- Thanks to the strong lineages of the House, the compact has produced many fine hunters, ones which were allowed to maintain double membership in other compacts or even conspiracies. While they joined all kinds of different groups (some have even awakened to the infernal lineage of the 7th Generation), they never forgot their shared origin. One day, when an ancient threat rose and endangered the world, it was the House who served as the linking chain which managed to unite many different groups together against it and banish it back to where it came from. Today, it still serves as the link between groups- and thanks to that neutrality, they gain access to the resources of their allies, both mundane and occult.<br /> <br /> Hunt Club- they have money, they have hierarchy, they have connection and members. However, falling into a Scourge Slasherhood is a constant threat for the members of the Club, which causes their own members to loose control and puts the Club in danger as whole. In order to learn how to control their murderous persona, they looked for ancient texts and found an Aztec tablet which taught them how to keep two faces- one for men and one for the gods. After learning how to keep their inner Slasher under control, they could have put a better use for their time- like culling the herd.<br /> <br /> I'll make the 4 Edo groups later :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T04:47:42-08:00","id":797747,"title":"","content":"Ama San- while time has passed, the tradition of the Ama kept on. Diving into the deeps, they used what they discovered there as a way to fund their humble community and protect their villages. Things changed when one of the prominent members of the compact dived deep enough to recover ancient treasures of a bygone age- the Tide Jewels of the Sea God, Kanju and Manju. Fearing the consequences of that power, Ryujin himself manifested before the community and asked for the Jewels, and the Ama San obeyed. Seeing the honesty and true spirit of the group, Ryujin's rage was replaced with joy. He took the jewels yet taught their ways to the group- the song of wave and storm. Under the Sea God's blessing, the group grew, absorbing similar compacts and eventually surviving into the modern days stronger than before.<br /> <br /> Azusa Miko- while Edo was an hard time for the Miko, the Meiji Restoration was worse. With the Emperor establishing new order through Japan, their practices were outlawed, leaving the group even more in danger. Under a common enemy, many former rival shrines united in secret, sharing the knowledge of both the spirits and the dead until they eventually developed the rites used to draw the Boundary and change the world with their sacred dances. Working from the shadows and gaining the support of their patrons, the group managed to survive until the fall of the Empire during the second World War. Since then, the group has started to grow back, and they don't plan to fall again.<br /> <br /> Bijin- since their foundation, all the Beautiful Ones asked for was gaining &quot;access&quot;, and while traditions rose and fell through the years one things remained constant- the lust of people for beauty and pleasure, and the Bijin knew how to provide it. For them, rising in the tiers was a calculated move, a necessary step to achieve their goal- until eventually, they collected enough favors and made enough contacts in order to create their dangerous Network. Now, they are the masters of social interactions- and no fly is able to escape their web of contracts and connections.<br /> <br /> Gimu- among all of the compacts of the Era, the Gimu had their hardest time before them. The rise of Meiji and the end of the Edo Era marked the end for the old tradition. While there were rebellions and attempts to fight the Emperor's control, eventually the government won- yet their spirit didn't died out. While they were publicly abolished, certain military officials kept true to the old code in their heart, and even without swords they kept watching the shadows for the influence of monsters. Losing the World War looked like the final blow for the few who carried the flame on, yet as time carried on people has started to romanticize about the old times. Even without a weapon, people turned their eyes back to the shadows and saw the monsters who hide inside of them. Eventually, the descendants of the old Gimu has started to build themselves together, united by those who climbed the social ladder thanks to hard work. Eventually, cooperation with Zen monasteries, they unlocked the secrets of mind and body, as far as they adhere to their Code. While they are not a big power among the 3rd Tier, they are still there- and they are still growing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T05:48:10-08:00","id":802024,"title":"","content":"and now a bit of fandom to fandom- Skin &amp; Bones's compact<br /> <br /> <b>Carvers- Persona (0-00000)</b><br /> Slashers view the world in a twisted way, and while that madness give them strength it could also be used as their weakness. That Endowment gives the hunter two benefits- first, it allows them to temporary rise their Integrity by spending one WP point per dot. You may not rise your Integrity more than your dots in the Endowment. The effect lasts until your next Integrity Breaking point, only that in case you fail that roll you don't lose Integrity or gain a Condition but simply return to your original score. That ability may be used only once per Chapter.<br /> <br /> The second ability is used in order to manipulate Slashers- by rolling [Persona]+[Integrity], you may activate one of the 3 effects- first, you may force a Ban upon the Slasher (Bane if Exceptional Success) supported by the mania of the killer for a Scene. Second, you may shut down one of the Slasher's Undertaking Talents for a Scene. Third, you may temporary rise the Slasher's Integrity by the number of dots in Persona, revealing him to his own horror. He suffer for -1 per dot in Persona for all rolls in the Scene. (except of Integrity rolls). Dramatic Failure would either force a Ban on you, make you more vulnerable to the Slasher's Talents or suffer the penalty yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Dirge- Last Blow Serum</b> <b>(0-00000)</b><br /> Killing what is already dead is not an easy job- but impossible, especially by using that serum! After years of research, the Dirge managed to synthesis that secret weapon out of Vitae and other exotic materials. In order to use the Endowment, you must first prepare a weapon by covering it with the fluid. That effect may enhance any mundane weapon (that is, not one enhanced by supernatural power), although in the case of ranged weapon the Serum must cover the projectile. You may not have more doses of the Serum than your dots in Status: [Dirge], and they are refreshed at the end of every Chapter. When dealing an attack against a living dead, the target suffers from an additional level of Aggravated damage which may not be healed for the rest of the Scene by any means. In the case of a melee weapon, the effect may be used again for a number of attacks equal to you dots in the Endowment. In the case of ranged weapon, each projectile may be used only once, by a single dose of the Serum may last for a number of projectiles equal to your Endowment. By ST's decision, you may buy dots in a separate Serum meant for other kinds of monsters other than Zombies, although they should cost a bit more than the usual (extra 1 exp)<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Cross- Neo Medicine (0-00000)</b><br /> while technology may create terrible weapons, it can also be used to heal. Using a cutting edge tech, the members of the Cross may stitch people up from pieces as easily as one may mold clay. While having access to their operation room, the hunter may add her dots in Neo Medicine into any medicine roll which allows her to heal a number of Bashing Damage equal to the number of Successes you get in the roll, a number of Lethal Damage equal to half of your successes or a single Aggravated Damage level. You may try the roll even without access to your operation room, but you suffer -2 penalty to rolls in case you have only an &quot;emergency kit&quot; or -3 if you don't have access to it. You get +1 modifier for every assistant you have (which must be someone with Medicine of 3 or above or someone with at least one dot of Neo Medicine) but that bonus may not be risen to more than +3 and only one person may attempt the roll in a single scene. In an addition, you may use Neo Medicine in order to heal supernatural diseases, conditions and even curses (as long as they don't remove a Major Template), but in order to do so you roll only Intelligence/Dexterity + equipment + Neo Medicine and must have access to an operation room. You may use Neo Medicine on the same target only once per Chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>Wordsmiths- Psychological Suppression (0-00000)</b><br /> the more powerful the monster, the human is the patient- that was the conclusion of the Wordsmiths. Using a special psychological technique, the therapist may strength the one on the expense of the other. While talking to the target, the hunter may roll Manipulation+Endowment against the monster's Potency score. Success would reduce the monster's Potency score by -1 per Endowment dot to the minimum of 0. A willing patient may not resist the roll, and than the Hunter just needs to Succeed- although Dramatic Failure would instead backlash and force the inner monster to attack the therapist. Exceptional Success would remove another dot of Potency. That effect lasts until the target's next Breaking Point, and a single target may not be effected by more than a single Suppression at a time. In case the therapist know the target, she gets +1 for rolls, and in case it is not her first &quot;treatment&quot; by the therapist she gains +2.<br /> <br /> <b>Sons &amp; Daughters of Cheshire- Disruption Field (0-00000, special)</b><br /> Relics are dangerous, for they act as keys for stranger realms- yet those are not the only keys in the world, and just as keys may open doors so they can lock them. By using the remains of shattered relics transplanted to their own body, the Cheshire Society is able to banish evil powers from the world and keep them on the outside. This Endowment may be bought a number of time, and each time be tied to another supernatural effect (like Unseen Senses). By spending a single WP point, the hunter may generate a field which blocks the effect of that phenomenon- any attempt to use an effect related to that phenomenon in a radius which equal or lesser than the hunter's dots in the Endowment in meters would require a Clash of Wills against the hunter or would automatically fail. In a case of a being which is not &quot;native&quot; to the world, that creature is banished back to its native world. In an addition, the hunter may seal interdimensional gates for a single Chapter by rolling Endowment+Willpower, when a Dramatic Failure would force the gate open and Exceptional Success would destroy the Gate (Failure gives -1 to any future roll on the same Gate until success of Dramatic Failure). The gate must be connected to the phenomenon which the Field is tied to.<br /> <br /> <b>Terra Incgonita- Cleaner (0-00000)</b><br /> using cutting edge technologies and questionable experiments, Terra Nullius has managed to develop a new botanic specimen which recycles the energy leaked from the Reanimated and use it to grow. Those plants, called Cleaners, may be GMOs, but desperate times means desperate means. Cleaners come in the form of seeds, until they are put inside a soil and are exposed to the Divine Fire of the Created. Once they are meant to be effected by Wasteland (or beings near them are exposed to Disquiet) the Cleaners start to grow, removing the Wasteland/Disquiet one level backward per dot in the Endowment. Any single Cleaner may absorb one such &quot;dose&quot; of Divine Fire until they reach their full Rating, and then they die out. Cleaners may also have a more &quot;active&quot; use- once having a direct contact with a Divine Fire Imbued Being (like a promethean, pandoran or even a qashmal) the plants start to grow without control, sending their roots into the flesh of their target. Each such Cleaner cause a single level of Aggravated damage per dot in the Endowment. Every hunter may have access to a number of seeds equal to 10*Status. A ST may allow the hunter to but different Cleaners for other phenomena (like vampires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-07-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:09:08-08:00","id":802151,"title":"","content":"Damn. I think the Cleaners stuck out the most for me. Beware &quot;flower power&quot;, lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T14:03:56-08:00","id":802335,"title":"","content":"I like how the Sons and Daughters of Cheshire can seal interdenominational gates. The last thing we want is easy passage between the Catholics and the Pentecostals! (The word you are looking for is &quot;interdimensional&quot;. Interdenominational means &quot;between two different religious denominations&quot;. I'm going to assume that spellcheck happened.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T21:42:27-08:00","id":802663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=802335#post802335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how the Sons and Daughters of Cheshire can seal interdenominational gates. The last thing we want is easy passage between the Catholics and the Pentecostals! (The word you are looking for is &quot;interdimensional&quot;. Interdenominational means &quot;between two different religious denominations&quot;. I'm going to assume that spellcheck happened.)</div> </div> </div> </div>and here I've thought my spellchecker stopped destroying my posts. I was wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T23:23:03-08:00","id":803596,"title":"","content":"<b>Narodnaia Volia- Anarchy (0-00000)</b><br /> False promises of freedom can only get you so far, and the hunger to disrupts unjust undead rulers can shatter every chain. While the blood of the Kindred is addicting, certain members of the group has developed tolerance toward it- and from there the rest is history. Each dot in Anarchy represent an additional step needed in order to form a Vinculum (that is, a member with 3 dots in the Endowment needs 6 drinks in order to become bound to a vampire). In an addition, by putting their hard won freedom in danger they may gain further power in fight against death's tyrants- by drinking a vampire's fresh Vitae, the hunter may gain access to a single Discipline the vampire has for the next 24 hours. The vampire only needs to know the Discipline in order for the hunter to use it, and the effective rating the hunter has in it equal's to the Endowment's rating. In order to power the Discipline the hunter may either spend WP points or cutting himself (inflicting Lethal Damage) equal to the cost of the Discipline (in case there is no cost, spend either a single WP point or deal a single Lethal Damage to activate the power). The hunter may not have two active Disciplines in the same time, and each time he wish to switch powers he needs to drink again another dose of Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:06:29-08:00","id":813632,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Cult of Mitra- Divine Fate (0-00000, Special)</u></b><br /> The human members of the Ivory Court protect their gods from the dark Daeva who seek to pull the Peri back to their iron cages, and Fate stands on their side when they do so. When taking the Merit the hunter choose a single Fate, which could be described in a single word (like Warrior, Scholar, Lover, etc). The hunter can use that Endowment in a number of ways- first, he can use that Fate to help them in their goal. By expanding WP point, the hunter may add her dots to a specific roll which works in the theme of their Fate (for example, a Warrior may add those dots when he attack seeking glory in battle, while a Lover would have to protect his special one from an enemy). Second, the hunter could roll her dots in a certain Fate in order to see the future- or, more exactly, her role in the story. She may add her Divine Fate dots to any Investigation roll which is meant to show her the preferred course of action considering her Fate, although she does not include the finale outcome of her role (including possible death). While the character may take more than one Fate, she must follow the theme of her chosen destiny- and if she defies it somehow (like a Warrior running away from battle) she would lose one WP point and would not be able to use that Fate for the rest of the Chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:51:06-08:00","id":814123,"title":"","content":"I personally don't think there need to be Endowments for every group. One of the greatest strengths of Hunter: the Vigil is the fact that it recognizes the existence of hunters without powers, both as individuals and groups, and that it gives us a distinction between groups with powers and groups without. I think that people who play these games get a little bit too hung up on the wikki powers and forget the rest of the character sheet. They forget that there are tactics, equipment, and other merits that could work to the player's advantage; many of which can be gained through role play.<br /> <br /> For example a lot of people seem to forget about Exorcisms and Abjurations as mentioned in the core rules book. Exorcisms and Abjurations are tactics that work like Endowments against ghosts, spirits, and demons, and would be used almost exclusively by The Long Night, being a Protestant Compact, and would resultantly make them a very effective compact against ghosts, spirits, and demons. I would not expect compacts like Null Mysteriis, Ashwood Abby, or the Bear Lodge, for example to use Exorcisms and Abjurations even if they knew about them. Even though Exorcisms and Abjurations are not hidden or secret knowledge, the knowledge of how to do them is different for different religions, and in some cases does in fact require specialized training. One example of this is the <u>real life</u> Vatican hunter conspiracy called the International Order of Exorcists (IOE). Seriously, it actually exists, go look it up. Every member of the IOE is flown to the Vatican in Rome to receive specialized training in the procedures, rites, rituals, and psychology of performing a proper exorcism. In fact, how the IOE hasn't made it into the Hunter RPG as a Vatican Conspiracy or Compact along side MM, I'll never know, but whatever. My point is there are other methods of having an organization leveling the playing field other than Endowments. Many Compacts may focus on training their members up in skills and tactics to level the playing field rather than developing Endowments. Bear Lodge might teach its members how to craft and lay traps for werewolves, like a bouncing betty land mine that sends silver shrapnel in every direction. It's not an Endowment, but it would work better on a pack of werewolves than a Doru relic.<br /> <br /> If you want your players to belong to a Compact, but still have powers or similarly awesome equipment to level the playing field, then may I suggest looking beyond Endowments and making the powers a part of your character rather than a part of the organization they are in. Take a look at Second Sight, and make some psychic powers as part of your character, rather than part of their organization. Or instead of making it part of your character, make it something they get through role play. Look into the Reliquary book, and have a non-Aegis Kai Doru hunter group (like Loyalists of Thule) go on a relic-based hunt that lands them a neat piece of equipment that they can use in a future story line. Aegis Kai Doru doesn't have to know about it. They may be a relic-centered conspiracy, but they are not all-knowing nor omnipresent. As for more mundane nifty equipment, if you want your werewolf hunters to have some big guns, have a look at the Armory book and see what some of the biggest guns are. If they want an AGTM missile launcher that does 20L damage, then let them go through the trouble of getting one on the black market to shoot the werewolves with. And I do mean all the trouble, including a possible visit from the FBI, which may or may not include the VASCU (which in turn could get your hunters conscripted into a VASCU suicide squad, which has role play potential of its own).<br /> <br /> My point is, let's not obsess too much over Endowments. They are only one aspect of the hunter game, and they are not even the most interesting aspect at that. As a friend of mine used to say, &quot;It's called role play, not roll play.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:11:11-08:00","id":814136,"title":"","content":"ammm do you mind to not turn this thread into a &quot;ideology thread&quot;? This thread is a mechanics thread, meant to STs who may want to turn a certain compact into a conspiracy according to the suggestions given in C&amp;C. It does not meant to make all compacts into conspiracies, or giving Endowments to all compacts. It is a brainstorming thread to &quot;what if&quot;, combined with some quick and dirty rules.<br /> <br /> In sort, I'm not saying that your view of the game is not valid- but I just don't understand why you posted it in here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T19:07:36-08:00","id":814591,"title":"","content":"Meh. Fair enough. I could elaborate on my reasoning, but I'd rather not open up a can of worms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:05:27-08:00","id":840909,"title":"","content":"so, let's talk Mystery Cults:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chosen of Mammon: Primal Utility (1-5)</u></b><br /> Money makes the world turn around, and everything has a price- and Mammon's faithful has the highest value coin to pay with. Primal Utility represent the sum of the connections and resources one gets thanks to the cult, allowing them to get their hands on anything they wish- for a sort period of time. That Endowment is a single, 1-5 merit, which act as some sort of Resources merit. However, instead of giving access for material wealth, it grants access to other merits: the cultist may get the effect of any merit which its rating is equal of lesser than her Primal Utility rating. That includes merits she usually does not have access to, like Supernatural Merits, other Endowments and even Merits meant for supernatural creatures. In order to get the Merit, the cultist must go through a &quot;purchase&quot; treatment- like going to the bank in order to get Resources or visiting some underground clinic for a psychic ability. The Merit is in effect for a number of days equal to their dots in Mystery Cult Initiation, and may not grant more Merit dots than the total rating of the Primal Utility.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Siblings in Arms: Big Guns (1-5, special)</u></b><br /> The Sisters of the Machine Gun and the Brothers of the Bomb has worked for long time in order to fight against the Machine and its loyalists. Using reverse engineering and understanding of the God Machine's occult matrices, they have developed a special kind of weaponry- one which may grant humanity the edge needed to escape the terrible will of its tyrant. Each Big Gun is a separate merit, doted 1-5, which hold a single Numina per dot. In order to activate the Big Gun, the cultist must feed it with Essence- that is, the type it is aspected to when created. The Gun in question has an Essence pool equal to its rating, and may regain Essence either as the aspected Ephemeral being or by being in the presence of the destruction of such being. Needless to say, most Guns are Angelic in nature, but more than a few are bound with ghostly or spiritual nature, if not weirder forms of Essence.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Fellowship of the Finale Answer: Anomaly (1-5)</u></b><br /> Seattle is a place where time shatter and resemble, and from those shards things may get out. Escaping their original timeline and ultimate fate, the demonologists has escaped their personal Hell and became into an anomaly on the face of the world. Anomaly is a single merit rated 1-5, which serves as some sort of &quot;Cover&quot; for the members, which masks them from agents of both Heaven and Hell, and each person who joins the cult becomes part of that anomaly. That Cover both works as a Supernatural Tolerance trait at an half of its actual value (rounded up) and allows them to Spoof as if its rating was equal to Cover. However, for the cultists Spoofing is a deliberate act- they can feel that something is searching after them or that perhaps they wish to make someone believe them no matter how weird is the lie they are going to tell. That act requires a Willpower point to do so. That &quot;Spoofing&quot; may also allow them to hide their thoughts or targeting them with sympathetic magic.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Church of Inti: Sunfire (1-5)</u></b><br /> The light of the Burning Star leaves no one untouched, and those who worship the idigam as Inti and survived are able to channel its heavenly Essence into their bodies as they hunt after those werewolves who dare to challenge their god. Sunfire is a single merit, rated 1-5, which allows three different uses- first, it acts as Influence: Fire with an equivalent rating, although instead of Essence it must be powered with blood, self inflicting one level of Lethal Damage per required Essence. Second, the cultist may activate it in order to engulf himself with such golden fire, something which requires one Willpower point and one level of Lethal Damage. As long as the &quot;Cloak of Fire&quot; is active, the cultist may interact with beings from the spiritual Twilight as if they were manifested, and even see beyond the Gauntlet. That power is active for one minute per dot in the Endowment. Finally, one can burn like a star, releasing all of Inti's Essence as a single, terrible blast. In order to do so, the cultist suffer one level of Aggravated Damage- and deals a number of levels of Aggravated Damage equal to his dots in the Endowment. For beings which are harmed by fire or sunlight, that damage is doubled. It is considered to be a ranged attack, with a range of one meter per dot in the Endowment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Voyagers: Kotoba no Kokai (1-5, special)</u></b><br /> words and blood are the will of humanity, and by ruling both one may extract control over both this world and its shadow. The cultist can make special ofuda written in their own blood, each is connected to a single Influence among the five Chinese elements which were adopted by the Onmyodo- that is, Fire, Water, Earth, Metal and Wood. In order to make such talisman, the cultist must self inflict a single level of Lethal Damage, and in order to activate it he must throw it on the target and spend Willpower point. When making the Talisman the hunter rolls for Crafts, when Failure destroys the Talisman and Dramatic Failure creates a flaw which can not be seen. Exceptional Success grants a Willpower point. Once the Talisman is activated, it creates the appropriate Influence where it touches. By ST's decision, other elements or aspects of reality may be invoked using the Endowment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tick Tock Men: Bioclock (1-5)</u></b><br /> The cult's obsession with the perfection of time has developed enough to create a new heart for its members- a clockwork machinery which always ticking, always measuring, always watching. Bioclock acts as a single, 1-5 merit, which channel the nature of time into their body. For every dot in the Endowment, the cultist may preform another action during her turn. While that power is terrifying, it does have a price- for the human mind and body were not meant to withstand such flow of time. After the end of the Scene in which the Endowment was activated (which requires a single Willpower point per use) the player has to choose whether to roll for Integrity with a -1 modifier per additional action taken during that Scene or suffering one level of Bashing Damage per such extra action.<br /> <br /> I think those are all the canon Mystery Cults- feel free to tell me if I missed someone! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:54:30-08:00","id":841924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zolace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=814591#post814591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. Fair enough. I could elaborate on my reasoning, but I'd rather not open up a can of worms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, this thread lets people rearrange which hunter groups have powers and which don't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T04:41:20-07:00","id":857055,"title":"","content":"so, let's add the new Dark Eras compacts to the list-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Keepers of the Weave- Tale Binding (0-00000)</u></b><br /> Stories are meant to protect those who hear them, as they give face and a name to hidden terrors found in the night. With a form given to such fears, the dream may become reality, and stories becomes a weapon to hold against them. Tale Binding is a 1-5 merit which allows the hunter to both gain information about a monster so they may discover its weakness. By rolling [Tale Binding] + [Intelligence] + [Occult], the hunter may draw upon mankind's collective conscious in order to find a story which describes the monster's existence and weaknesses, giving them both the general information about their target and +[Endowment] modifier to every attack roll against that monster. By preforming [Tale Binding] + [Presence] + [Expression] roll, anyone who hears that story enjoys that bonus as well. Dramatic Failure would make it the wrong story, giving you or your friends -[Endowment] modifier, while Exceptional Successes also grants a Willpower point to anyone who hears the story while fighting the monster.<br /> <br /> A more interesting effect of the Endowment comes when the hunter tries to force a Tale upon the monster, forcing a persona upon it. In order to do so, the hunter must roll [Tale Binding] + [Manipulation] + [Expression] and expand a Willpower point against the monster's supernatural tolerance as normal. If the hunter wins, the monster is no under the spell- as long as the hunter keeps preforming the story, the monster suffers from -[Endowment] modifier as it start suffering from sudden memories of thoughts which does not belong to it but of the being the story tales, and the hunter may also choose a single weakness which would deal Aggravated damage to it. Those effects may only target monsters.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Protectors of the Light- Ward (0-00000)</u></b><br /> The Protectors live together with the land and know it better than anyone else- they respect it, and in return it gives them a shard of its power in order to cleanse it from the foul monsters and keep the light shining. The Ward is a single, 1-5 merit which establish a connection between the hunter and the land. Each dot in the Endowment gives the hunter a different ability, as detailed bellow-<br /> <br /> 0- Mind's Eye: the hunter can feel any material being in a radius of 1 meter per dot in Presence, although she doesn't know its identity, intentions or if it is a supernatural being.<br /> 00- Earth Bound: the hunter may add a single dot to a Physical Attribute for free. It may not rise an attribute above 5.<br /> 000- Spirit Sight: the hunter may now recognize beings in the Twilight, recognize if a being is a supernatural or not and discover if it is hostile, friendly or indifferent.<br /> 0000- Land Keeper: the hunter may add another dot to any attribute she wish for free. The hunter may rise an attribute above 5.<br /> 00000- Life's Fountain: the hunter enjoys Regeneration, as a Warden (see Immortals), may project his mind into the Twilight to scout her territory (as in Mind's Eye) by spending a Willpower point per hour (she may change frequencies by spending another) to interact with the beings in there and may transform blood into Essence to bargain with spirits (presented by self inflicting Lethal Damage).<br /> <br /> In an addition, the hunter gets one free Environmental Tilt per dot in the Endowment. By spending a Willpower point, the Tilt comes into effect in a range equal to the hunter's Presence, although she must spend a Willpower once per 10 minutes to maintain it. She may activate a number of such Tilts in the same time. Anyone who is not a member of the Protectors of the Light is effected by such Tilts. There is, however, a downside to the Endowment- for as the shard of light in the hunter grows, such her body becomes tied more and more to the land- by taking the first dots in the Endowment, the hunter limits herself to a specific region, and that regions becomes tighter and tighter as time pass by. Once leaving that region, the hunter lose access to her abilities, and suffers Lethal Damage as detailed below-<br /> <br /> 0- a Continent, 1 LD per year<br /> 00- a sub-region, 1 LD per month<br /> 000- a country, 1 LD per week<br /> 0000- a district/state/metropolis/region/any other sub-nation division, 1 per day<br /> 00000- a city or a similar community/territory, 1 per hour<br /> <br /> the ST is the one to approve if a certain territory answers the demands. Traveling through mental projection outside of such territory is allowed, in case she has enough Willpower. For each dot in presence the hunter has, she may extend her territory by 1 km and postpone the damage by 1 time unit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:57:01-07:00","id":911624,"title":"","content":"and now- the Aztec Mystery Cults:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cuauhualtin- Ihhuitzoncalli (0-00000)</b></u><br /> The Eagle Warriors of the empire wear the shape of their companion as a crown and soar to the sky, granting them part of Quetzalcoatl's majesty. In order to use that Endowment, the warrior must form a blood bond with a companion eagle, which must be renewed once every 260 days. While renewing the bond with any eagle would do, most prefer to keep a long connection with a single companion because of the spiritual and emotional connection which is created during the ceremony. That Endowment is a single, 1-5 merit, which is based around the companion eagle as a medium for its powers. As long as the duration is active the Endowment could be used by expanding a Willpower point, although certain abilities may require the warrior to have a living companion to use. The abilities gained through that Endowment are:<br /> <br /> 0- Emphatic Link: the warrior may telepathically commune with his companion and instinctively know its location.<br /> 00- Sky Sight: the warrior may extend his senses beyond his body and into his companion, allowing him to see through its eyes and hear through its ears.<br /> 000- Feathered Form: the warrior can take the form of an eagle by himself, as if he had the Skinthief merit.<br /> 0000- Wind's Shield: when taking an eagle form, the warrior enjoys the benefit of Resilient Form Merit with a rating equal to the Endowment.<br /> 00000- Blessing of the Quetzalcoatl: the warrior may channel a shard of his god's true form, giving him the Hybrid Form merit for free.<br /> <br /> In an addition, having even 1 dot in the Endowment counts as having the Skinthief merit in order to buy dots in Essence Pool and Spirit Powers, with his animal form being counted as the &quot;flayed spirit&quot;<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ocelomeh- Cehualli (0-00000)</b></u><br /> The Jaguar Warriors stalk the shadows of the empire and run through the forest's darkness as living shades. In order to use that Endowment, the warrior has to have access to a jade jaguar talisman and self inflict one level of Lethal Damage before use. Once activated, the warrior and all of his gear are transformed into an half solid, black shadow in the form of a jaguar. During that form, the warrior may target beings both in the Twilight and the material world, although he may only be harmed from supernatural sources. Spirit or ghost specific abilities may not effect his form, although shadow twisting abilities may cause him harm. During that form, he may use his dots in [Status: Jaguar Warriors] as an Honorary Rank against either ghosts or spirits (decided during the transformation). The warrior may stay in that form for 10 minutes per dot in the Endowment, although the duration may be extended by inflicting another level of Lethal Damage. In that state, the warrior use the Ephemeral Being rules for Attributes, and he may also buy and use Dominions by expanding Willpower for activation.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nahualtin- Tezcatilpoca (0-00000)</u></b><br /> The world is found in constant movement, always changing and transforming. Even the gods take part of that cycle, and by looking in a smoking mirror one could become a god. That Endowment is a single, 1-5 merit which serves as an &quot;energy state&quot;- for each dot in the Endowment, the cultist gains a single dot of Source which may be expanded in order to activate Mysteries as if he was a witch. In an addition, for every dot in the Endowment the cultist gets one free dot in a Mystery. In order to replenish his Source, the hunter must cause 2 Lethal Damage per point either to himself or to a sacrifice. He may only regain Source that way, and can only activate Mysteries by using Source. He does not suffer from Paradox at 5 dots, yet any witch can recognize that the spells cast him are &quot;tainted&quot;, and the same could be seen from his Aura. Also, that taint has certain extra side effects- each time the cultist rolls for Integrity Breaking Point, he suffer a -[Endowment] modifier for the roll.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Huitzilopotchli the Many Wheeled- Tonalpohualli (0-00000)</u></b><br /> All goes in cycles, and that which happened would happen again. What Rise must fall, what's fallen may rise again. In the movements of the wheels inside wheels, the cultists of the Sun may see what is bound to happen, and by invoking the days of the sacred calendar their gods would answer. That Endowment is a single, 1-5 merit which has a number of uses- first, it is used for divination. By dealing a level of Lethal Damage to a sentient being, the cultist may enter into a trance and see the future as if she had the Omen Sensitivity merit with using the Endowment instead of Wits. The act requires access to the calendar in order to use. Performing a human sacrifice before the activation of that power grants +2 modifier.<br /> <br /> Second, that merit gives the cultist the ability to twist space and time. That ability is a passive effect, which helps the cultist during times of battle, shifting time in split seconds in order to escape a deadly hit or create invisible boundaries which may not be crossed. In order to enjoy that effect, the cultist must either inflict Lethal Damage to sentient being, he may add his dots in the Endowment to either Attack rolls or Defense for the next Scene (chosen during activation). That effect may not be changed until the end of the Scene, and only one such effect may be used at the same time.<br /> <br /> Finally, the understanding of the wheels of the world grants the cultist the ability to use some of his god's greatest gifts. First, the cultist gain a single Numina which could be powered with Willpower or Lethal Damage to sentient beings for each dot in the Endowment. Second, at 1, 3 and 5 the cultist gains and single Incept for free as if he was an angel. The hunter may buy additional Numina as if they were merits, but may not gain further Incepts. When a certain incept calls for an angel's Rank, use the Mystery Cult Initiation's rating instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-10-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:47:30-07:00","id":912170,"title":"","content":"and for the upcoming Compacts in Beast's Mortal Remains, I present-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Yuri's Group- Lifebond (0-00000+)</u></b><br /> People are afraid when they feel alone- when there is no one to support and help them, they are an easy prey to the nightmares lurking in the shadows. Together, however, they are able to preform great feats, showing those nightmares that they are nothing more than illusions made by their own minds. Lifebond is a single, 1-5 merit which allows the hunter to form deep, subconscious bonds with other individuals. The hunter may maintain a number of those bonds equal to the Endowment's rating, and establishing such connection requires a physical connection between the hunter and the target. Such Lifebonds could be shifted at any moment. Alternatively, the hunter could make such connection into permanent Lifebond, which requires buying it as a separate 1 dot merit.<br /> <br /> Once the Lifebond is established, the hunter gains the ability to strength his bound using his soul and willpower- every time the target needs to spend a Willpower point, the hunter may decide to spend one in her place. Plus, every time that target requires rolling Willpower or a Breaking Point, the hunter may allow her to use his traits instead for the roll. The hunter, on the other hand, can use the number of active Lifebonds as a Supernatural Tolerance Trait (not including permanent ones), and it gives him an additional amount of Willpower points equal to that number. Many of the hunters of the Group use the Endowment to support each other and help new recruits to deal with their traumas, but more than enough has chose a beast or a similar monster as a Lifebond in order to help it maintain its hunger and rehabilitate it from its old habits.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Reckoning- Reverentia (0-00000, special)</u></b><br /> All looks at the Lord's majesty with awe, and those who fear God's wrath are the ones to understand His divine plan. Those who forsake that fear are doomed to rebel against the Lord's will like Nimrod did- and like him, they will be doomed by that hubris. Each Reverentia is a single, 1-5 merit which draws power from the primordial fear man feels when meeting one of God's divine creations, and turns it into a weapon against those who stand before the Lord in twisted sense of pride. There are five types of Reverentia, each is based around invoking one of God's Archangels which channel that divine awe against their enemies, each reminds how useless you are without God on your side- Gabriel (who without him all is hopeless), Uriel (who without him all is dark), Selaphiel (who without him all is hidden), Raphael (who without him all is broken) and Michael (who without him none are safe).<br /> <br /> In order to activate a Reverentia, the hunter has to spend a Willpower point and roll [Reverentia]+[Presence] minus the target's [Resolve]+[Composure]. In case the conditions fit the Endowments themes, that hunter gains a +2 modifier (that is, activating Uriel in the dark, or Raphael near an old building). That modifier goes to +3 if the conditions resonant with the Archangel's sphere (Gabriel on an high place, or Selaphiel near the sea). In a case of Success, the target suffer from the Spooked Condition as she experience the Archangel's true form (Uriel whispers from the shadows, Michael watch from the heavens, etc), and suffer one level of Bashing Damage per [Reverentia] as the boundaries between the Divine and the physical become blurred. Exceptional Success turns the Condition into Shaken. Dramatic Failure would turn God's wrath upon you, making you to suffer from the Spooked Condition and a number of Bashing Damage levels equal to [Endowment]. Reverentia can even effect beings who are normally immune to fear unless it was done by using some active power. God's majesty effect all of his created, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T16:06:41-07:00","id":945727,"title":"","content":"so in the Strange Alchemies sidebar in the PtC 2e book, there was a certain discussion about how alchemists and hunters interact with each other, giving some organizations which are likely to work with alchemists- however, let's explore the possibility of alchemist organizations which work with hunters and the strange gifts they may gain from it. While alchemist is a temple on its own right, we do have conspiracies which do alchemy (the AO as canon example)- so there is some precedent for it. Anyway, I've decided to use only those groups which have some &quot;higher reason&quot; to hunt prometheans other than refining them into pyros- may it be the word of god, dedication to old tradition or even simple profit, those groups may have interest at recruiting regular people to their structure in order to carry their mission, creating a true hunter group around them. I may work the others in similar way because there are not a lot of them if I'll be bored enough or if someone would ask for it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lodowick Society- Divine Vision (0-00000)</u></b><br /> Prometheans are beings of stolen life, souls taken from God by force of madness. Such abominations, and other beings and people who try to steal God's fire, has to be destroyed- and the Divine sends its vision to guide his loyal followers in battle. The character may preform an Elpis Vision as if she was a promethean. Such Elpis Vision are always preformed as if they were forced by the character, and require meditation using christian symbolism (such as the Cross, images of Saints, meditating about heaven, etc). Considering that the character lacks Azoth, use the Endowment's dot rating instead. The hunter may only ask questions about the Vigil or phenomena which are related to the Divine Fire. As hunters lack connection to the Azothic Memory, both the Success and the Exceptional Success are identical to the regular Elpis Vision roll, while Failure acts as the regular Elpis Vision's Dramatic Failure. Dramatic Failure stays the same- the hunters of the society may be blessed by God, by you can't play with fire without getting burned.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Pristine Order of Auric Chalice- Aludel (0-00000)</u></b><br /> Only the worthy should use alchemy, and only they may work the miracles of the Divine Fire in secret- but the common people still has their use, and may gain some of the Fire's finished products as long as they serve the alchemists in hunting those unworthy to the that power. Each Aludel is a small object, usually in the form of an orb, containing sparks of the Divine Fire inside of it, and has a 1-5 rating. The hunter may only carry a number of Aludels equal to her Status [Conspiracy] rating- that means that a hunter with 5 dot Status may either carry a single, powerful Aludel or 5 weak ones. The hunter may change her armory by visiting one of the Order's bases.<br /> <br /> Each Aludel is based around of the aspects of Pyros- Elpis and Flux. Elpidian Aludels give access to any Dsitilation (other than those of the Flux Transmutation), using the Aludel's dot rating instead of Azoth, together with spending a Willpower point. The hunter must touch the Aludel in order to activate it. While using the Transmutation effect is the most common one, there is another effect, used only in emergency- releasing the Divine Fire to the world. Doing so requires destroying the Aludel, which is then treated as a Firestorm Catalyst, with a number of success equal to double the Aludel's rating. The Firestorm's Aspects should be decided in advance. The effect is activated automatically once the Aludel is broken. While the other may replace the Aludel freely, destroying too many Aludels may cause fall in Status.<br /> <br /> The other type of Aludels are Lilithian Aludels- each of those Aludels is based around a Flux Dsitilation, and activate as Elpidian Aludel. However, when destroyed, they create the effect of a Jovian Athanor for a number in a radius of [Aludel] meters, which is decided in advanced. The effect lasts for a number of minutes equal to the Aludel's rating double 2, and is focused around the place where the Aludel was destroyed. The user is not immune to any of the effects caused by destroying the Aludel.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Amalgama Ltd- Transhuman Potential (0-00000)</u></b><br /> Amalgama's specialty is biotechnology, and it equips its specialized mercenaries with dangerous powers to help it forcing other alchemists into its web and destroy targets asked by costumers. Transhuman Potential is a single, 1-5 merit, which require the character to got through a harsh procedure to adapt her body to the mutating effects of Pyros- or, more exactly, Flux. By spending a Willpower point and rolling Stamina+Composure, the character may gain temporary access to Pandoran Dread Powers with a total rating equal to her dots in the Endowment. Dramatic Failure would cause her a number of Bashing Damage levels equal to her dots in the Endowment as the Flux mutate her body without control. In case a Dread Power requires Pyros, use Willpower instead. The powers remain in effect for a Scene, although the character may prolong it with expanding another Willpower point without having to roll once more. The character's body is mutated because of the effect appropriately to the powers manifested. The hunter may end the effects of the Endowment at any time.<br /> <br /> and while it is not an alchemist guild- Sheriff Brown's deputies are hunters in all but the name, so here is their possible Endowment!<br /> <br /> <b><u>Phoenix Fire Guard- FP (0-00000, Special)</u></b><br /> The Fire gets out of control, and monsters go out of it. They scorch the earth as they walk and break souls and minds in their wake. In order to protect the people, one has to fight that fire- and put it down for good, so not even embers would be left behind. FP- or Fire Protection- is actually three sets of merits, each having a different 1-5 rating. PFP, or Passive Fire Protection, stops the passive effects of the Fire upon the community. In order to activate the merit, the hunter must spend time at &quot;fire proofing&quot; a place with an area of 10*[PFP] m^2, an act which requires hour hour per 10 m^2. Working with other hunters who act as supporters remove 30 minutes per hunter, yet no less than half an hour. Once protected, all individuals in the area may add the PFP's rating to any roll to resist a Disquiet effects, and Wasteland Festers as if it was one level lower and Fades as if it was one level higher.<br /> <br /> The second Endowment is called AFP- or Active Fire Protection. Using specialized equipment (such as special fire extinguishers), the hunter may harm the promethean and its powers. Use AFP as a ranged weapon, with every promethean effected by it suffer a number of Aggravated Damage equal to its rating. Each AFP can be used for a single Scene, and after which the hunter has to get a new one from the office. In addition, and active Transmutation effect which meets an AFP causes a Clash of Wills using [AFP]+[Phoenix Deputy] against the effects of the Transmutation. In case the AFP wins, the Transmutation ends automatically.<br /> <br /> The last Endowment is Fire Suit. As long as the hunter wears the special suit, she adds her Endowment's rating to any attempt to resist the effects of a Transmutation used upon her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:41:40-07:00","id":947023,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the information about the Voyagers Mystery Cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:11:45-07:00","id":947045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=947023#post947023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find the information about the Voyagers Mystery Cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition, at the Tokyo setting (p. 272)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:58:40-07:00","id":959360,"title":"","content":"<b><u>White Heart </u></b><b><u>Pharmaceuticals- Paranormal Infections (0-00000)</u></b><br /> Through ages of research and work with supernatural beings, the company has developed a number of powerful pathogens for various uses- and through special vaccinations, only those members of the conspiracy are immune to its side-effects, turning them into ideal carriers of the occult diseases which simply wait to be unleashed. Paranormal Infections is a single, 1-5 Endowment, with each dot representing a single pathogen the character is carrying inside of her. Each such infection is designed as a 5 stages effect, with each stage granting a single Condition or Tilt to the infected and stages 2-5 each has a special &quot;trigger&quot; which cause the infection to go up one step. In order to infect a target, the hunter ha to touch the target and spend a WP point. Alternatively, exchanging blood with the target would always infect the other individual (the hunter may instead take a air-spread version of an infection, but it is considered as 2 dots of the Endowment). To resist the infection, the target has to roll for Resolve+Stamina against the character's Manipulation+Endowment. Supernatural beings which are normally immune to diseases still needs to roll, but may add their Supernatural Tolerance trait. Once infected, the target would suffer from the Condition/Tilt of the first stage and the disease would progress normally. Each time it does, the infected may resist the pathogen, but suffers a -[stage] modifier to the roll. Treating the infection requires either a supernatural treatment or gaining the serum from the conspiracy. The hunter herself is immune to any pathogen she carries, and to any none supernatural disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:02:31-07:00","id":959906,"title":"","content":"White Heart Pharmaceuticals? Are they another Alchemist guild from Promethean 2E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:06:40-07:00","id":959907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=959906#post959906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Heart Pharmaceuticals? Are they another Alchemist guild from Promethean 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>nope- they are a company presented at Falling Scales as the power behind a number of cults, compacts and occult societies. They mainly develop all kinds of vaccines and such, and has some deep connection to occult, especially the Egyptian kind, and are outright said to have contact with some of the most ancient monsters of CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:43:27-07:00","id":959930,"title":"","content":"Ahh. And is Falling Scales a Dark Eras chapter? I can't recall whether or not it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T12:09:59-07:00","id":959946,"title":"","content":"Falling Scales is a two part SAS for the general CofD setting, made especially for mortals (although it includes options for adapting it to all gamelines up to Geist), which goes around mortals revealing the supernatural and the secret maneuvers preformed by the company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T03:28:12-07:00","id":960968,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Emerald Crucible: Amulet of Eternity (0-00000)</u></b><br /> Unlike other alchemists, the Crucible are not a selfish group- their goal is helping humanity as whole to transcend the limitations of their physical body and stave off death. While alchemists could gain such gift through their research of the Fire and harvesting the humors of prometheans, most of mankind are not alchemists- and those who help them in their hunt gain some of their gifts. The Amulet of Eternity is a single, 1-5 merit which takes the form of a physical object, usually made out of emerald. The Amulet itself acts as a container of supernatural energy, requiring the user to &quot;charge it up&quot; to make it useful. In order to do so, there are two ways- the first is investing Willpower points into the Amulet (it can't hold more Willpower than its rating). The second is by using the humors of a promethean, which usually requires the help of an alchemist at dissecting the monster and harvesting the Fire from it. Doing so replenish the Amulet's energy ton its maximal amount.<br /> <br /> Once the Amulet was charged, it has the following effects- first, as long as it holds at least one point of energy in it and is held by the hunter, she would not age. Removing the Amulet would make her rapidly age to her chronological age. Second, the effective amount of energy invested in the Amulet is treated as a Supernatural Tolerance trait to help the hunter fight supernatural effects. Third, and most important, the energy of the Amulet could be used in order to enhance the hunter's body and transcend her usual limitation. By spending a single energy dot from the Amulet, she can either enhance one of her Attributes by one for the next Scene, heal one level of Lethal Damage, remove a single personal Tilt which is caused by physical or mental harm or suppress a Persistent Condition for a Scene. The Amulet can by charged at any moment by spending the Willpower cost. All such effects require a physical contact between the hunter and her Amulet.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Order of the Four Cornered Seal: Gu (0--00000)</u></b><br /> after years of investigating poisons, sickness and madness, the alchemists of the cursed Order learned how to disrupt their own, natural harmony into creating an artificial imbalance by refining special poisons out of vermin- poisons which grant their hunters both power and curse. The practice of Gu requires an alchemist to preform the traditional ritual (trapping venomous vermin together and let them kill each other until only one is left) and extract the refined poison. The hunter then consume the poison and roll for Stamina+Gu to resist the effects. In case of failure, he suffer from one level of Lethal Damage (Dramatic Failure turns it aggravated, for not only the poison wasn't refined but also charged with dangerous occult energy). In case of Success the hunter may choose any Dread Power whose rating is equal or lesser then her Gu rating. Mixing the poison with promethean humors grants +2 modifier for the roll. Once manifesting the same power 4 times in that way, the character may choose to turn it into a permanent power, which takes the form of a black tattoo shaped like the animal which was used for the ritual. The effective rating of all permanent Dread Powers can not be greater than her Gu dots, although she may switch such Powers with new ones after following the conditions, which creates new tattoos but won't remove the old ones. Temporary Dread Powers last for 10*[6- Dread Power] minutes once the poison is taken, and use Bashing Damage is fuel for their effects. Each Dread Power, both permanent and temporary, force a negative Condition or Personal Tilt upon the character as long as it is in effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 08-31-2016, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T05:20:02-08:00","id":1031098,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Titgwai Gang- Gisei [0-00000]</u></b><br /> The gang worship the ghost goddess of the train stations, giving her sacrifices in exchange for future gain. Those sacrifices allowed the Tek tek to grow in power, and she fulfilled her part of the deal. Gisei is a single, 1-5 merit, symbolizing the strength of connection the hunter has with the sacrifices she gives to herself. Once sacrificing a desired object through burning (as the traditional sacrfices for the dead) the cultist may then roll for Gisei+Occult+Manipulation. In case of Dramatic Failure, the Tek tek shows her displeasure, blocking the use of the Merit for a number of hours equal to 6-MCI. In case of Success, the cultist may spend one Willpower point in order to call upon the object for a number of days equal to her Gisei. In case it was a weapon, the summoned object deals Aggravated damage. Those items may interact with the Twilight. The cultist may also decide that instead of gaining the item itself he prefers to gain a more abstract benefit. In case of Success, you get the benefit of a single Merit for the duration of the Endowmet, with a rating equal or less than your Gisei. You may not have two such Merits active in the same time. Sacrificing a kishamono gives you +2 for the rolls. Exceptional Success would give you one such temporary Merit dot. Supernatural items destroyed through Gisei could be accessed even after the duration has ended, considering the roll was successful.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Precinct 44- Auctoritas [0-00000]</u></b><br /> Authority, not truth, makes the law, and the bad cops of Precinct 44 know to to use theirs. Whenever preforming a Social Maneuver, you may spend a Willpower point in order to lower the amount of needed Doors by [Endowment]. In an addition, the cop may roll for Endowment+Manipulation and expand a Willpower point. In case of Success, the target treats fearing the cop as a Vice and obeying him as an Aspiration. Exceptional Success gives him a point of Willpower. Dramatic Failure makes the character immune to the influence of Auctoritas. Finally, when forcing a door, the cop may use half of his Endowment (rounded up) as a modifier for the roll.<br /> <br /> still thinking about the other Violent Groups. Some of them are pretty hard to do, as they are clearly not player material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T05:10:20-07:00","id":1142468,"title":"","content":"so after a long time of no updates, I present potential Endowments for hunters who work with the different Sekhem Sorcerers, as well as the Tomb Raiders from Mortal Remains<br /> <br /> <b><u>Order of the Bull (a.k.a Taurans)- Calls of Earth (0-00000, special)</u></b><br /> The priests of Sarruma the Mountain King know the ways of the earth and can evoke its power to their help. Each of the Calls is a separate, 1-5 merit which calls upon the aspects of the ground beneath their feet. A sorcerer may not try to activate one of the Calls in case their body does not directly touch the ground, and suffer -2 modifier in case they stand upon a &quot;stone conduct&quot; (such as activating it in a building while standing above ground floor), and +2 in case they are beneath the ground (like in a cave, or in a sewer). The Calls themselves are represented in the form of Influences, with all of them being tied either to earth (like sand, stone, mud, etc) or things are are connected to earth (plants, graves, fortitude, etc). The ST is the one to decide whether a certain Call is appropriate. In order to activate a Call, the sorcerer has to roll for [Call]+[Manipulation] and spend a special resource known as Chthonic Force. A sorcerer may only spend 1 Chthonic Force per turn, yet in order to activate a Call they must pay a number of point equal to its rating. Dramatic Failure would cause a Call effect equal to the one the sorcerer wished to preform, but it would turned against the sorcerer instead. Exceptional Success gives the sorcerer the Inspired Condition, as the might of the world's bones fill their body. The sorcerer has an a Chthonic Force pool equal to their Stamina+Resolve, and may only spend one point per turn. Regaining Chthonic Force requires participating in one of the harsh rituals of the cult (full refill), by meditating upon earth (one dot per Success) or claim it from another sorcerer which is bound to you as Chattel. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Adelfoi Aimatos- Blood Curses (0-00000, special)</u></b><br /> The blood assassins are well known for their deadly arts, and their combination of physical harsh training and strange sorceries, they can bring death to their enemies with a blink of an eye. Each Blood Curse is a 1-5 merit, based around a single Condition or Tilt, including supernatural ones. In order to activate a new Blood Curse, the sorcerer needs to have access to two things- a drop of blood from the target and know their true name (not True Name). Once the ingredients are ready, the sorcerer may activate the Endowment by rolling [Curse]+[Occult]. The roll suffers from -1 modifier per 1 km which separates between the sorcerer and the target, and costs one point of Lethal Damage from the caster. In case of Success, the Condition/Tilt is immediately enforced upon the target for one hour per dot in the Curse. Exceptional Success also steals life from the target, dealing them Lethal Damage while healing the cot the sorcerer paid for the act. Dramatic Failure, however, creates the opposite scenario, with the sorcerer suffering another Lethal Damage while the target heals it (or gains a Willpower point, if they are already fully healed).<br /> <br /> <b><u>\u200bLoyalists of the Ptolemaic Dynasty- Entombment (0-00000)</u></b><br /> The heirs of the Osiris Reborn cult seek to cross the boundary between the living and the dead in order to become like the undead gods they serve, and by spending a night among the dead they can mimic that divine glory. Entombment is a single, 1-5 merit which represents the ability of the sorcerer to cross the line between which separates life and death and transcend them both. In order to activate that power, the sorcerer has to spend a day and a night in a tomb next to a corpse and roll for [Resolve]+[Composure] by the end of the night. In case of a Dramatic Failure, the sorcerer's mind has managed to pierce the veil, yet it was maddened by the horrors to which it was experienced. Gain the Broken Condition. In case of Success, the sorcerer's body is transformed by the experience, as Sekhem rush into their body and infuse it with unnatural gifts. The sorcerer may gain any Affinity which its Pillar prerequisites is equal or lower the Endowment's rating, when the total rating of all Pillars needed for the Affinities is equal to the sorcerer's Entombment. The sorcerer may access those Affinities for a week before they require preforming the ritual once more, even though they may try again if they wish to change their Affinities. Failure in such attempts would remove the access the sorcerer previously had. Exceptional Success also gives the sorcerer a single Clue or a Willpower point. While the sorcerer may try once more using the Entombment ritual, using it too early damage the mind of the user- doing it more than once a week is considered a Breaking Point with a negative modifier which is equal to the number of the days which are still needed to use the ritual &quot;safely&quot; divided by 2, rounded up. Sorcerers may only access Soul Affinities using Entombment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Parangelia Seth- Isfet (0-00000)</u></b><br /> The time the cult has spent with the Lifeless and the prophesies they gained from their patron has taught them all kinds of dark secrets unknown to the common men. By invoking their patron's Name and Will, they can cause awaken the wild powers of Sekhem into life, and trap those wild energies into physical form. Isfet is a single, 1-5 merit which can be used in order to create temporary relics. By rolling [Isfet]+[Craft] and paying a Willpower point, the can cause the local Sekhem to crystallize and solidify into an item. The created relic can mimic any existing mimic or have new powers of its own, yet it does not carry a curse. In order to activate a certain relic, the sorcerer must use a command word which was decided during the item's creation. The effect lasts for a single Scene. The relic may be used for a number of times equal to the sorcerer's Endowment before the occult power fades away. Gaining an Exceptional Success while creating the relic allows the sorcerer to use the relic twice as much, while Dramatic Failure enforce a Curse upon the sorcerer which lasts for one day per [Isfet]. At any case but Failure, however, the Curse is activated upon anyone who enters the place the relic was created for as long as the relic still exist, for the act defiles the world around it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Circle of the Stars (a,k.a the Strangers)-</u></b><b><u>Golden Apple (0-00000, special)</u></b><br /> The ancient order of the Strangers has learned to movement of the heavenly bodies and their influence upon the River of creations and destruction, and by invoking the right stars, names and gods, they may tap upon the energies which flow in the world and use them to enhance their chosen Hero. Golden Apple is a single merit, rated 1-5. Each Endowment represent a certain recipe, and which its finale outcome is a potion which could enhance any fruit with a supernatural power. When designing the recipe, choose both the needed ingredients and the powers which are contained in the ritual- which is a combination of Affinities and Dread Powers which their total rating and Pillar prerequisites may not be higher than the Endowment's rating. The ingredients needed for a certain recipe always require a Resources rating equal to that of the Endowment (with one of them always being a small piece of an mummy's flesh of a shard of a relic), while the process of making the potion requires rolling [Occult]+[Intelligence]. Dramatic Failure would make the potion into poison, causing one point of Bashing Damage per dot of the Endowment, while Exceptional Success would also give the one to eat the Apple a Willpower point. Once eating the Apple, the user gains access for all the powers contained in the fruit for the rest of the Scene, even though they need to pay any Willpower cost needed for them.<br /> <br /> and now, for hunters-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tomb Raiders- Dream Gate (0-00000)</u></b><br /> While the Tomb Raiders are still small, many great things wait for them in the future thanks for the secret they managed to uncover- the ability to open Dream Gates to the Lairs of a Beast. In order to activate a Dream Gate, the hunter in question must at least know to where they plan to go. In case of a random Lair, they suffer from a -3 modifier for using the Endowment. In case they only know the Beast's general appearance, they suffer from a -2. In case they know their name, they suffer from -1. In case they are in close proximity to the Beast, they suffer no negative modifier. The place where the Gate is opened must be of the same nature as the target's Lair. The act itself requires rolling [Endowment]+[Manipulation]-[Target's Lair]. In case of a Failure, the Beast immediately knows that someone tried to enter their Lair, and in case of Dramatic Failure they also know where they are. Success would allow entering the Beast's Lair, but the Beast is still aware of the break. Exceptional Success means that not even the Beast knows their defense was compromised. Once in the Lair, the hunter may collect any material or artifact from the Lair, even though they may not carry out more than one item per Intelligence dot. Those items (or the items made from the stolen resources) hold each a single Dread Power based upon the Beast from which they were stolen, and may be incarnated in the real world. The hunter may open the Gate in order to leave the Lair without any roll, but it has to be opened from the inside just from the same place it was open from the outside- meaning going back from where they first entered the Beast's inner world- and must be opened by the same person which created the original portal. A Gate may be opened by another person or in another location, but it requires another roll and it suffers from a -2 modifier, for the Begotten has much greater control on their Lair from inside of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T07:53:12-07:00","id":1477527,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=LostLight;n911624] for every dot in the Endowment the cultist gets one free dot in a Mystery.<br /> <br /> <br /> i don\u2019t understand what you mean by this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/blob:http://forum.theonyxpath.com/30ff2a5d-ff5b-4dec-8fca-50f9a75f97ea\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <br /> \u201cwhat in the goddamn?\u201d -benny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26749-mothstrigoi","name":"Mothstrigoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T13:38:21-07:00","id":1477546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=911624#post911624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for each dot in the Endowment, the cultist gains a single dot of Source which may be expanded in order to activate Mysteries as if he was a witch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries are part of the Gutter Magic system presented for modeling witches in Hunter the Vigil: Witch Finders.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}